{
  "requirement": "Evidence inputs MAY have a definition form containing exactly `definition` and `text`. `definition` MUST identify one named definition; `text` MUST contain its complete raw fenced declaration as source lines, including its phrase option and explanatory body.\n\nValidation MUST reject missing definitions and changed snapshot text, identifying the definition and showing a compact diff when available. Moving an unchanged definition within its chapter MUST NOT invalidate its snapshot. Evidence displays MUST show the definition name, current source location, and recorded text.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The marked tests cover each obligation in `requirements.definitions.inputs`.\n\n**Form: exactly `definition` and `text`.**\n- `tests/definitions.rs#fn[definition_schema_deletion_and_literal_references_are_checked]` adds an `unexpected` field to a definition input and asserts an \"unexpected field\" error.\n- `fn[changed_definition_snapshots_show_a_compact_diff_and_text_is_required]` removes `text`, sets it to `[]`, and sets it to a string. It asserts an `evidence/rules.ready.json` error mentioning `text` in each case.\n\n**`definition` identifies one named definition.**\n- The same test adds definition inputs naming a requirement (`rules.ready`) and an example (`rules.case`). It asserts a \"no matching named definition\" error for each.\n- `src/evidence.rs#mod[tests]/fn[configuration_and_dependency_failures_do_not_stop_later_checks]` records `rules.gone` and asserts an `inputs[0]` error saying there is no matching named definition.\n\n**`text` is the complete raw fenced declaration, including the phrase option and body.**\n- The test helper `declaration` builds the text independently of the implementation, from the opening `:::{...}` line to the closing `:::`.\n- Validation of those recorded inputs passes in `fn[cyclic_dependencies_are_required_once_and_changes_require_review]`, so the fences are part of the compared text.\n- A change to only `:phrase:` and a change to only the body are each rejected as \"input text changed\", in `fn[cyclic_dependencies_are_required_once_and_changes_require_review]`.\n\n**Validation rejects missing definitions.**\n- Deleting `md/glossary.md` gives an error naming `glossary.a` with \"no matching named definition\", in `fn[definition_schema_deletion_and_literal_references_are_checked]`.\n- The `rules.gone` case above also covers this.\n\n**Validation rejects changed snapshot text, identifies the definition, and shows a compact diff.**\n- `fn[changed_definition_snapshots_show_a_compact_diff_and_text_is_required]` asserts the error names `glossary.a`.\n- It asserts the diff is exactly one removed body line and one added body line.\n\n**Moving an unchanged definition within its chapter does not invalidate the snapshot.**\n- `fn[cyclic_dependencies_are_required_once_and_changes_require_review]` prepends blank lines to the glossary. This shifts every definition's location without changing its text.\n- It asserts validation reports no errors.\n\n**Evidence displays show name, current location, and recorded text.**\n- `src/index.rs#mod[tests]/fn[detail_page_shows_recorded_text_locations_and_first_matching_group]` has a definition input with recorded text `recorded term`. That text differs from the source, so the display must be using the recorded snapshot.\n- It asserts the detail page shows `definition rules.term`, then the name with its current file and line range, then the recorded text block, in that order.\n\nI found no unaddressed obligation or assertion gap.",
  "references": "b55f37e0df05544f95f7bea68aad31a6abff40adc5e6252b5aa3542a6897bcc5",
